  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Member</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, the Member is a combination of introversion, intuitiveness, we-centeredness, and calmness. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to speech-language pathology, middle management, and human resource. With their interdependent nature, Members can blossom in these paths. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/speech-language.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Speech-Language Pathology</h5>
              <p>Speech-language pathology is one of the most unique career paths that you can pursue. And above all archetypes, you are the most gifted to pursue this path given how well you connect with others.</p>
              <p>Generally, language is one’s gateway to the world. Without the ability to speak, expressing oneself is greatly compromised. Unable to express themselves to the world, kids who lack the ability to speak are prone to being misinterpreted or even discriminated by peers who don’t know any better.</p>
              <p>Your task here is truly one of a kind. By helping children (and even adults) build their confidence and guide them how to express themselves to the world, you become the catalyst that invokes change.</p>
              <p>But in order to do this, you need a special skill – the ability to deeply connect with your clients. And of all the archetypes, the Member is the one whose most adept at doing this (perhaps only rivaled by the Caregiver).</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>By spending more time with them, you develop an intricate bond of trust. Expressing their vulnerability to you, these patients will see you as someone that they can closely work with. And as you guide them through, you’ll improve certain aspects of their speech abilities such as fluency and voice.</p>
          <p>Coincidentally, doing this will allow you to realize a bigger purpose. As your actions have turned into concrete results, you will see your relevance to the world. Becoming a part of improving someone else’s life (and earning well, too), you are able to live out the goal of being a Member archetype.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/human-resource.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Human Resource</h5>
              <p>With your ability to create solid a solid connection to your team, a career on the human resource is out of the question. Tasked to coordinate, assess, and evaluate the employees of the company, a human resource person is at the heart of what makes the company tick. In fact, this career even deals with the unsightly aspects of the company, signifying the importance of your role.</p>
              <p>In essence, this stems from two gifts – realism and interdependence. In order to become a strong human resource person, these two qualities are strongly needed.</p>
              <p>Without a doubt, your sense of realism allows you to see things for what they are. Instead of making some biased judgment towards a favored co-worker, such realism allows you to see who’s truly at fault. This, of course, leads to sound judgment when dealing with conflicts within the company.</p>
              <p>And with that, you will gain the respect of your colleagues. Impartial and unbiased, they will trust that you’ll make decisions that are for the best interest of the company. By establishing your respectable position, such trust will even bolster the culture of interdependence.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Finally, pursuing this career path allows you to play a significant role in the bigger whole. Like a glue that holds everything together, your passionate and unwavering determination to make the best decisions for everyone will shed light to your archetype. As you become a great human resource person, you’ll embed yourself in a role that’s truly irreplaceable.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/middle-management.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Middle Management</h5>
              <p>Often, one of the problems with middle management is the promotion of Silo mentality. As various teams and its members decide to withhold information to other teams, such crippling logic often prevents the company to achieve its best interests.</p>
              <p>Similarly, such toxic traits are present among middle managers who see themselves as bosses instead of leaders. Constantly abusing their power, these middle managers satiate themselves by letting out their stress on those below their ranks.</p>
              <p>But with your unrivaled dedication to a culture of trust and interdependence, you are highly unlikely to become a rotten middle manager. Instead, there’s a great chance that you’ll be the one to sow the seeds of cooperation and mutuality within the company.</p>
              <p>As such, you are able to live out your gifts while being of value to the company you’re working with. And for the Member, this is a perfect scenario to move forward. Flapping your wings forward, you become the very chain that keeps everything in-tact.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>More importantly, your interpersonal skills also help you prevent internal strife. As your intuition grants you the power to see through things, you can prevent conflict even before it happens. Such acumen is highly valued for it ensures that everything remains balanced within the workplace.</p>
          <p>And as you do these things, people will simply love you for it. They will feel recognized instead of simply being cogs in a machine. In turn, your passion and dedication actualizes into something that brings appreciation back to you.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span>, and it is this...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
